// Unrecoverable aborts. Like `%ref`, this is a single function rather than a record:
// `%panic "message"` aborts the current process. It imports nothing, so every other module
// can use it, which is also why the message is typed as `Str['bin]` rather than `'%str`.
#Str['bin] {
  :doc """
    Aborts the current process with the message. A panic is a bug rather than a failure, so it never
    returns and can't be recovered from locally. A process awaiting this one answers nil with a
    `Panic[pid, message]` `:crash` payload.
    """
  __panic__ $
}
